1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,682
Creating a tenant by hand means filling in forms, one after another.

2
00:00:05,682 --> 00:00:10,554
A workflow can create a tenant and set it up from values you type once.

3
00:00:10,554 --> 00:00:15,110
In this video, we build one, run it, and open the site it creates.

4
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:25,601
The Tenants module adds four activities to the workflow designer, in the Tenant category.

5
00:00:25,601 --> 00:00:28,019
Create Tenant Task adds a tenant.

6
00:00:28,019 --> 00:00:33,290
Setup Tenant Task sets it up, with a site name, an administrator, and a recipe.

7
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:38,742
Disable Tenant Task switches a running tenant off, and Enable Tenant Task switches

8
00:00:38,742 --> 00:00:40,291
a disabled one back on.

9
00:00:40,291 --> 00:00:43,871
Each of the four has a Failed outcome, which it takes when it

10
00:00:43,871 --> 00:00:45,100
can't do its job.

11
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:48,628
Each activity checks its tenant first.

12
00:00:48,628 --> 00:00:53,994
Create Tenant Task needs a name that no tenant uses, and an address of its own.

13
00:00:53,994 --> 00:00:58,160
Setup Tenant Task needs a tenant in the Uninitialized state.

14
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:03,433
Disable Tenant Task needs a Running tenant other than the Default one, and

15
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:06,203
Enable Tenant Task needs a Disabled tenant.

16
00:01:06,203 --> 00:01:10,670
All four activities work in the Default tenant, which manages the others.

17
00:01:14,970 --> 00:01:17,435
The activities need two features.

18
00:01:17,435 --> 00:01:23,060
Open Tools, Features, search for Tenants, and select Enable on the Tenants feature.

19
00:01:23,512 --> 00:01:27,094
Search for Workflows, and enable that feature too.

20
00:01:27,094 --> 00:01:32,082
The admin menu then lists Multi-Tenancy, Tenants, and Design, Workflows.

21
00:01:36,382 --> 00:01:39,590
Open Design, Workflows, and select Create Workflow.

22
00:01:39,590 --> 00:01:43,474
A workflow only needs a name, so let's call this one Create and

23
00:01:43,474 --> 00:01:44,712
set up a tenant.

24
00:01:45,184 --> 00:01:48,415
Under More settings, clear Record activity data.

25
00:01:48,415 --> 00:01:53,441
It keeps the values each activity evaluated, in the journal of every instance,

26
00:01:53,441 --> 00:01:57,031
and this workflow will hold an administrator password.

27
00:01:57,031 --> 00:01:59,844
Then select Create and open the designer.

28
00:02:00,294 --> 00:02:02,817
The designer opens on an empty canvas.

29
00:02:02,817 --> 00:02:07,347
A workflow starts with an event, so we search the activities for Started,

30
00:02:07,347 --> 00:02:11,533
and add Started By Workflow, which becomes the start, marked Start.

31
00:02:11,533 --> 00:02:15,604
The designer's Run button can run a workflow that begins with it.

32
00:02:19,904 --> 00:02:24,548
Select Done on Started By Workflow, search for Create Tenant, and pick Create

33
00:02:24,548 --> 00:02:26,954
Tenant Task from the Tenant category.

34
00:02:26,954 --> 00:02:29,864
Its settings open at the bottom of the canvas.

35
00:02:30,319 --> 00:02:35,066
We type Bluebird in Name, and again in Description, so the tenant's name

36
00:02:35,066 --> 00:02:37,500
and its description read the same.

37
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:41,699
The Url Prefix, bluebird, gives the site an address of its own.

38
00:02:42,156 --> 00:02:46,455
For What type of database to use, type the provider's name, Sqlite.

39
00:02:46,455 --> 00:02:50,048
For Recipe, type the name of a setup recipe, here Blog.

40
00:02:50,048 --> 00:02:52,286
The other fields can stay empty.

41
00:02:56,586 --> 00:03:01,062
Select Done on Create Tenant Task, and add Setup Tenant Task.

42
00:03:01,062 --> 00:03:06,206
Its Tenant name is Bluebird again, and its Site name is Bluebird Books.

43
00:03:08,869 --> 00:03:15,239
Admin user name, Admin email, and Admin password describe the administrator of the site:

44
00:03:15,239 --> 00:03:19,169
admin, owner@example.com, and a password you choose.

45
00:03:19,624 --> 00:03:23,866
The database fields and Recipe stay empty, so the task uses what Create

46
00:03:23,866 --> 00:03:26,069
Tenant Task stored for the tenant.

47
00:03:26,069 --> 00:03:30,311
The workflow stores the admin password as plain text, so anyone who can

48
00:03:30,311 --> 00:03:32,294
edit the workflow can read it.

49
00:03:36,594 --> 00:03:37,832
Select Publish.

50
00:03:37,832 --> 00:03:43,314
The designer saves your changes as you work, but a workflow runs its published version.

51
00:03:43,772 --> 00:03:46,568
Select Run, and Run again in the dialog.

52
00:03:46,568 --> 00:03:52,342
Setting up the site takes a moment, and then the dialog reports the Instance as Finished.

53
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,238
Open the instance.

54
00:03:54,238 --> 00:03:58,674
The page highlights the activities and connections the instance ran:

55
00:03:58,674 --> 00:04:02,810
Started By Workflow, Create Tenant Task, and Setup Tenant Task.

56
00:04:07,110 --> 00:04:13,920
In Multi-Tenancy, Tenants, Bluebird is listed with its description, its database, Sqlite, its

57
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,810
recipe, Blog, and the state Running.

58
00:04:17,273 --> 00:04:19,451
Select its name to open the site.

59
00:04:19,451 --> 00:04:23,248
It answers at the Url Prefix we gave it, and shows the content

60
00:04:23,248 --> 00:04:24,643
of the Blog recipe.

61
00:04:28,843 --> 00:04:33,620
A task that takes Failed leads nowhere unless you connect that outcome.

62
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:38,769
With no connection, the workflow ends there, and the instance reads Finished.

63
00:04:38,769 --> 00:04:43,793
Connect Failed to an activity such as Log or Notify, to report the problem.

64
00:04:44,543 --> 00:04:50,666
Run this workflow a second time, and Create Tenant Task takes Failed, because Bluebird exists.

65
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:55,380
Disable Tenant Task and Enable Tenant Task need only a tenant name, and

66
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:58,563
any event can start a workflow that uses them.

67
00:05:00,563 --> 00:05:04,432
A workflow can create a tenant, set it up, and later disable or

68
00:05:04,432 --> 00:05:06,955
enable it, all from the Default tenant.

69
00:05:06,955 --> 00:05:08,413
Thanks for watching.

